{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a19f30d8176c4b20",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -480,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Multi-Pass Rendering Pipeline\n\nData is not saved at `End*Pass()`.\n\nDraw calls write into the currently bound RTV. `End*Pass()` usually only unbinds outputs/resources."
    },
    {
      "id": "d2e7a1b4c8f59033",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -520,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 2920,
      "height": 520,
      "label": "Frame Data Flow",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4c62a971e0f83ad",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -460,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## HDR Pass\n\n`BeginHDRPass()`\n\nRTV = `m_hdrRenderTexture->m_renderTargetView`\n\nDSV = `m_depthStencilDSV`\n\nScene geometry is rendered here."
    },
    {
      "id": "ce4d90281a6b7f35",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -80,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## HDR Scene Texture\n\n`m_hdrRenderTexture`\n\nStores the full scene color in HDR.\n\nLater passes sample it as SRV."
    },
    {
      "id": "f83a27c06d51b49e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Bright Pass\n\n`BeginBrightPass()`\n\nRead = `m_hdrRenderTexture`\n\nWrite = `m_brightPassTexture`\n\n`DrawFullQuad()` runs bright-pass shader over every pixel."
    },
    {
      "id": "a7c3f6b8e9120d45",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 680,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## Bright Texture\n\n`m_brightPassTexture`\n\nStores only bright pixels.\n\nDark pixels are usually black."
    },
    {
      "id": "e91b04ac5728df63",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Horizontal Blur Pass\n\nRead = `m_brightPassTexture`\n\nWrite = `m_horizontalBlurTexture`\n\nBlur happens left/right."
    },
    {
      "id": "c0a87359bf142e6d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1440,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## Horizontal Blur Texture\n\n`m_horizontalBlurTexture`\n\nStores the bright image blurred horizontally."
    },
    {
      "id": "f60e31b9a4c82705",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1820,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Vertical Blur Pass\n\nRead = `m_horizontalBlurTexture`\n\nWrite = `m_verticalBlurTexture`\n\nBlur happens up/down."
    },
    {
      "id": "b7d5e1840c9a632f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2200,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "## Bloom Texture\n\n`m_verticalBlurTexture`\n\nFinal blurred bright image.\n\nTone mapping samples this as bloom."
    },
    {
      "id": "d94e1f3b680ac725",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2580,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 320,
      "height": 190,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "## Tone Mapping Pass\n\nRead = `m_hdrRenderTexture`\n\nRead = `m_verticalBlurTexture`\n\nWrite = `m_renderTargetView` / backbuffer\n\nHDR + bloom becomes screen color."
    },
    {
      "id": "ea62c57091fb348d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2980,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 140,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "## Screen / Backbuffer\n\n`m_renderTargetView`\n\nThis is what `Present()` shows."
    },
    {
      "id": "ad37284e90b16c5f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "## `DrawFullQuad()`\n\nDraws a screen-sized quad so the current pixel shader runs once for every output pixel.\n\nIt is a post-process trigger, not a world-space object."
    },
    {
      "id": "f1e5ab903c7d2468",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 360,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "## Pass End\n\n`End*Pass()` usually unbinds SRVs and RTVs.\n\nIt prevents read/write conflicts when a texture changes from output to input or input to output."
    }
  ],
